        "title": "Lesson 2 | History of Muwaṭṭa",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we delve into the life and trials of Imām Mālik ibn Anas, focusing on his interactions with powerful figures like Abū Jaʿfar al-Mansūr and his steadfast commitment to preserving the teachings of the Prophet (PBUH). We discuss the famous incident where Imām Mālik was lashed for his fatwā on coerced divorce, and despite the immense physical pain, he continued to utter \"اللهم اغفر لهم فإنهم لا يعلمون\" (O Allah, forgive them, for they do not know). His resilience in the face of adversity became a symbol of his dedication to truth.\n\nWe also explore his unique approach to combining ḥadīth and fiqh, and the lasting impact of his masterpiece, Al-Muwaṭṭāʾ. Renowned scholars like Al-Shāfiʿī, Ibn Wahb, and Ibn Mahdī praised his work, with some even claiming there is no book more beneficial to the people after the Qur'ān than Al-Muwaṭṭāʾ. Join us as we uncover the remarkable story of Imām Mālik and his monumental contributions to Islamic scholarship.",
        "topic": "Imām Mālik and Al-Muwaṭṭaʾ",
