      {
        "portalId": "6fc8b2eb-0504-473e-ad37-413a64a1d7fc",
        "title": "Lesson 18: The Types of Water",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we cover the first two conditions for the arkaan of wudhu: that it be with water, and that the water be unrestrcited.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "a0708376-478e-4826-8a97-a76579d587ab",
        "title": "Lesson 19: How does water become restricted?",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we cover the two methods in which water becomes Muqayyad. The Mazhab has prefered al-Zayl'i's view in this, whihc was explained from his texts as well as al-Haskafi's text. We contrast this wih al-Quduri's text in the Mukhtasar and al-Marghinani's explanation in his Hidayah.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "74a3cdde-fd88-4d45-bdd2-3f98df210eb7",
        "title": "Lesson 20: How does water become impure?",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we covered a detailed discussion on how water becomes impure. We discuss the difference between this and water becoming restrcited, followed by an explantion of Quduri's text, as well as how the later commentators have misunderstood it.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "5bb6d376-32b8-4fe7-a119-843899b734fd",
        "title": "Lesson 21: How does water become impure? Part 2",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we continue our discussion on how water becomes impure. After this, we cover if water becomes impure by an animal dying in it.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "981176e2-67e1-4e05-8130-ed10c33de342",
        "title": "Lesson 22: Used Water Part 1",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we discuss the fourth condition, that water not be used. In doing so, the causes that result in water being used, as well as the time when it is determined to be used is discuss.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "66d587f5-2e0f-4781-ba7d-3332fa8648f5",
        "title": "Lesson 23: Used Water Part 2",
        "overview": "In this lesson, the discussion on used water is continued, followed by the reasoning behind the different views and the ruling of using such water for wudhu. Al-Quduri's definition of used water is presented, and finally, the third cause presented by al-Kamal Ibn al-Humam.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "3f35a771-a80a-43df-95d3-cb3b1cfdccee",
        "title": "Lesson 24: Animal hides, bones, and hair",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we cover the remaining discussions in the rulings on Miyah, specifically the ruling of purifying animal hides. Thereafter, al-Quduri mentions the rulings on bones, hooves, muscles, and other parts of an animal. At the end of the lesson, an extensive summary of Masa'il al-Miyah is given, spanning over restricted water vs. unrestricted water, impure water, and used water.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "01ec34ee-3b56-4025-b0dc-60cc2f9f377a",
        "title": "Lesson 25: Purifying Wells Part 1",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we cover the inital discussions on purifying well. Two Qiyas's in the chapter were mentioned along with the Istihsaan, followed by a detailed explanation of the first line in the chapter.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "3f4565c6-22fb-4185-8455-8e8b456d6c7e",
        "title": "Lesson 26: Purifying Wells Part 2",
        "overview": "In this lesson we continue with the remaining rulings regarding well water.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "6990f7da-4ae3-4a8d-9e1d-99bc3672734f",
        "title": "Lesson 27: Leftover Water Part 1",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we cover the rulings of leftover water. An important section is dedicated to understanding why washing a dish thrice is sufficient to purify the dish of a leftover dog, and why a cat's leftover water is makruh.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "d118b14c-09ac-4a46-9d87-ef334f41d2a8",
        "title": "Lesson 28: Leftover Water Part 2",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we continue on with the rulings of leftover water. The lesson shows the depth of Fiqh and the genius of the Fuqaha, as well as explains Istihsaan and Qiyas in detail, with a practical application of both.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "be0c5a75-2c50-4904-b84c-4c29e2cdf169",
        "title": "Lesson 29: Leftover Water Part 3",
        "overview": "In this lesson we complete our discussion on leftover water. We explain the ruling of water leftover by a donkey or mule in detail, followed by a summary of the two previous discussions.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "b3c07e76-853b-4346-9a11-063797e3a6e0",
        "title": "Lesson 30: Intro to Tayammum",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we introduce Tayammum. After discussing the definition of Tayammum, we discuss one condition of Tayammum in detail: the inability to use water.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "1b1a430a-5340-4d01-ac5b-97dab16ff678",
        "title": "Lesson 31: Tayammum Part 2",
        "overview": "In this lesson we explain the first two texts of al-Quduri, discussing over 7 different rulings that can be understood from the texts. Each ruling is discussed in thorough detail, along with due attention being given to the views of the later scholars of the school.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "d721e900-04b7-421a-a6ec-7a3a5154f054",
        "title": "Lesson 32: Tayammum Part 3",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we cover a detailed explanation of al-Quduri's third line. The explanation discusses the four scenarios in which a person can do tayammum out of fear of cold. Each scenario is discussed in detail, along with an explanation of Abu Hanifah and his students' views.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "d0b8017c-2281-4c9f-851e-3380459d48f1",
        "title": "Lesson 33: Tayammum Part 4",
        "overview": "In this lesson we cover a few more reasons that permit Tayammum. Although the author has not mentioned these in his Mukhtasar, the Hanafiyyah have mentioned them in detail. After this, the method of Tayammum was discussed, along with an important discussion with regards to whether striking the earth is an integral component of Tayammum or not.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "0d452d47-8227-49b6-9c85-906cad10d3d3",
        "title": "Lesson 34: Tayammum Part 5",
        "overview": "In this lesson we continue to discuss what Tayammum can be done with. The khilaf of Abu Hanifah and Muhammad, and then the larger khilaf with Abu Yusuf is mentioned. A detailed discussion on 'aam and takhsis with practical examples is visited in the discussion.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "d6b97bee-cac5-4d89-86db-5ae1190d39fb",
        "title": "Lesson 35: Tayammum Part 6",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we move on to discuss the condition of Niyyah in Tayammum. Unlike wudhu, Abu Hanifah and his two students feel that the Niyyah is a condition for the validity of Tayammmum. The reason for this is mentioned, followed by a discussion on exactly which Niyyah is sufficient in Tayammum.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "3975e78e-da5d-4e5b-b98b-b6915b928b7b",
        "title": "Lesson 37: Tayammum Part 8",
        "overview": "In this lesson we cover when a person should delay Salah if Tayammum is permissible for him, and when he shouldn't.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "1960d26c-be36-46b5-8f72-d0c2cf7fe1e7",
        "title": "Lesson 38: Tayammum Part 9",
        "overview": "In this lesson we cover when it is required for a person to search for water prior to praying Salah, and when it is not necessary to do so. In the case where it is required, the distance he is required to cover searching for water is also mentioned.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "6e03b861-5ade-4a7f-b21f-9b137d266151",
        "title": "Lesson 39: Tayammum Part 10",
        "overview": "In this lesson we continue to discuss another permitting cause of Tayammum: the fear of missing a Salah which has no alternative. We explain that this refers to Salat al-Janazah and al-Eidain with certain conditions, and discuss the method in which the mashayikh explain these rulings and riwayat in detail.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "7369213e-f287-4d88-ace9-375f0891653c",
        "title": "Lesson 40: Tayammum Part 11",
        "overview": "In this lesson we cover the situation where a person fears he will miss Jumuah or a Fardh Salah, will he be allowed to do Tayammum or not? The lesson covers the view of our three A'immah as well as the view of Imam Zufar, followed by the khilaf between Tarafan and Abu Yusuf where a person forgets he had water with him.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "abb64dc3-042d-406d-b73a-f9d664601dac",
        "title": "Lesson 41: Tayammum Part 12",
        "overview": "In this lesson we cover the last portion of Tayammum, revisiting the mas'aha of Talab and then moving onto when a person must request water from his companion.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "e5c9435d-18ef-47a0-80c9-778a7260d0d2",
        "title": "Lesson 42: Wiping the Socks: Ruling and Conditions",
        "overview": "In this lesson we cover the rulings pertaining wiping over the socks. We begin with Quduri's first text in the chapter, explaining how he mentions both the ruling and the conditions pertaining to the one wiping over the socks. The two conditions that are discussed in detail are that the wiping be from Hadath Asghar and that it be on complete purity. The second condition is discussed in detail as al-Quduri's text in the Mukhtasar is not the most clear regarding the condtion.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "26c0f3ca-948c-4839-9df3-59b176f1c01c",
        "title": "Lesson 43: Wiping the Socks: Place and Time Period",
        "overview": "In this lesson we move onto discuss the time period and the place of wiping over the socks. The first consists of three different discussions: the valid area, the method, and the required amount, each explained thoroughly with multiple rulings exrracted from them.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "3fbfeefe-f9ec-4fa1-9c92-37998599b937",
        "title": "Lesson 44: Wiping the Socks: Tears in the Khuff Part 1",
        "overview": "",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "c8f042a0-22ee-4223-9fb2-5af1127ac592",
        "title": "Lesson 45: Wiping the Socks: Tears in the Khuff Part 2",
        "overview": "",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "f4b8dec2-e983-4f19-a6f4-50b1ff3a7ee9",
        "title": "Lesson 46: Wiping the Socks: The Invalidators",
        "overview": "",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "f6398d58-0482-45b7-9b18-dd05be10239a",
        "title": "Lesson 47: Wiping the Socks: The Leather Covering",
        "overview": "",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "cb181d53-33a2-487b-b00a-5a9480d07b0f",
        "title": "Lesson 48: Wiping the Socks: Types of Socks",
        "overview": "",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "8915c5dd-5d51-4df4-b2ce-c3b3ac7be223",
        "title": "Lesson 49: Wiping the Socks: The Cast Part 1",
        "overview": "In this lesson we begin discussing the rulings of wiping over the cast or bandaid.",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "69572d07-5b03-4ae8-90be-2567dab7b632",
        "title": "Lesson 50: Wiping the Socks: The Cast Part 2",
        "overview": "",
        "topic": ""
      },
      {
        "portalId": "2979e52c-03f8-4b2a-9322-b9a620463e53",
        "title": "Lesson 51: Summary Part 1",
        "overview": "In this lesson, we begin our summary of the previous discussions.",
        "topic": ""
      }
