        "overview": "Naṣb has five signs: fatḥah, which is the default, alif, kasrah, yā, and the deletion of the nūn, all of which stand in the place of the fatḥah. The fatḥah is used for naṣb in the singular noun, whether munṣarif or not, in the broken plural, and in the fiʿl muḍāriʿ when a nāṣib enters and nothing follows it. The alif is a sign of naṣb in the six special nouns. The kasrah is used instead of the fatḥah in the sound feminine plural and what follows its rule. The yā appears in the dual and what is attached to it. Finally, the deletion of the nūn marks naṣb in the verbs whose rafʿ is by the nūn.",
