    "learningOutcomes": "• While the work is compiled in Arabic, the course will be conducted in the English language, making it accessible to a wider audience of interested students. This bilingual approach ensures that learners can engage with the material effectively, regardless of their primary language.\n• However, a foundational knowledge of basic Arabic is essential, particularly for some discussions presented at the beginning of the course and throughout the sessions. This familiarity with Arabic terminology will enhance students’ understanding of key concepts and enable them to fully appreciate the nuances of the text.\n• By bridging the linguistic gap, the course aims to foster an inclusive learning environment that encourages participation and enriches the educational experience for all students.",
