        "overview": "The lesson discusses an important section from the work Tadrīb al-Rāwī fī Sharḥ Taqrīb al-Nawāwī by the eminent scholar Jalāl al-Dīn al-Suyūṭī (d. 911 AH). In this section, al-Suyūṭī presents a discussion about the historical development of the written literature of Muṣṭalaḥ al-Ḥadīth, particularly addressing the question: Who was the first scholar to compile a book dedicated to the principles of ḥadīth science?\nThe discussion includes quotations from major scholars such as Ibn Hajar al-Asqalani, and engages with scholarly debates regarding manuscript readings, editorial methodology, and the chronological development of early works on ḥadīth methodology.",
