        "overview": "This lesson focused on an important and advanced discussion in the sciences of ḥadīth criticism (ʿulūm al-ḥadīth), namely the methodological differences between the scholars of ḥadīth (al-muḥaddithūn) and the jurists (al-fuqahāʾ) in determining the authenticity of narrations and identifying hidden defects (ʿilal). The discussion revolved around statements attributed to the great scholar Ibn Daqīq al-ʿĪd and comments found in later works such as Bayān al-Wahm wa al-Īhām and the marginal notes (ḥawāshī) of later scholars.\n\nThe central issue discussed was whether every hidden defect (ʿillah) identified by the scholars of ḥadīth must also be considered a defect according to the principles of the jurists. The lesson demonstrated that the methodologies of the two disciplines are sometimes different, even though both ultimately seek to preserve and correctly understand the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.",
