    "learningOutcomes": "• Students will engage in a comprehensive linguistic analysis of the Tā'iyyah, focusing on key elements such as iʿrāb (grammatical analysis), vocabulary enhancement, and the practical application of grammar (naḥw) and morphology (sarf) rules. This meticulous approach will not only sharpen their analytical skills but also deepen their understanding of the Arabic language.\n• Course Benefits:\n• 1. Linguistic Proficiency: Through in-depth examination of the poem, students will refine their grasp of Arabic syntax, expanding their ability to construct and deconstruct sentences with greater precision and confidence.\n• 2. Vocabulary Enrichment: The course will introduce a wealth of new vocabulary, allowing students to expand their lexicon and enhance their expressive capabilities in both written and spoken Arabic.\n• 3. Practical Application: Students will learn to apply grammatical and morphological rules in practical contexts, ensuring that theoretical knowledge translates into real-world language use.\n• 4. Broader Insights: Beyond the linguistic aspects, the course will draw broader insights from the verses, connecting the themes of the poem to everyday life and the transformative journey of seeking knowledge. This holistic approach will help students see the relevance of their studies in a larger context.\n• 5. Exposure to Classical Literature: By working through the Tā'iyyah, students will not only appreciate its literary beauty but also gain insight into the depth of classical Islamic literature, enriching their cultural and intellectual horizons.\n• This course is ideally suited for students who already possess a foundational understanding of Arabic and are eager to deepen their knowledge and appreciation of the language and its rich literary tradition. Through this journey, students will emerge with enhanced linguistic skills and a more profound connection to the themes that have inspired generations of seekers of knowledge.",
