        "overview": "This lesson belongs to the broader discussion of al-Sunnah within uṣūl al-fiqh according to the Ḥanafī school. Its primary focus is the concept of khabar al-wāḥid (singular report) and the conditions under which such a report is considered ḥujjah (legally authoritative). The lesson clarifies that the Ḥanafī approach to ḥadīth evaluation is not identical to the methodology of the muḥaddithūn (ḥadīth specialists), and that many modern misunderstandings arise from conflating uṣūl al-fiqh with uṣūl al-ḥadīth.\nThe discussion also addresses historical developments in Ḥanafī legal theory, the role of early scholars such as ʿĪsā ibn Abān and al-Jaṣṣāṣ al-Rāzī, and the allegation of Muʿtazilī influence. Throughout, the lesson emphasizes that theoretical principles must always be evaluated in light of actual legal application (furūʿ), not in isolation.",
