        "overview": "The science of Uṣūl al-Fiqh (أُصُولُ الفِقْهِ, uṣūl al-fiqh) provides the methodological foundations through which Islamic legal rulings are derived. Among its most significant discussions is that of Qiyās (القِياسُ, al-qiyās), often translated as analogical reasoning.\nQiyās represents one of the most powerful intellectual tools in Islamic jurisprudence. It allows jurists to derive rulings for new situations not explicitly addressed in the Qur’ān or Sunnah, by identifying the effective cause (ʿillah) behind a known ruling and extending that ruling to comparable cases.\nAlthough often placed later in classical uṣūl manuals, Qiyās is essential for understanding the dynamism and adaptability of Islamic law. This lesson presents a structured and corrected academic explanation of Qiyās, clarifying its definition, legitimacy, components, conditions, and limits.",
