        "overview": "In this lesson, the discussion continues on Qiyās (analogy) after completing its conditions (الشروط). Now we turn to its arkān (pillars) — the essential components without which Qiyās cannot exist.\nThe scholars traditionally mention four pillars:\nAl-Aṣl (الأصل)\nAl-Farʿ (الفرع)\nḤukm al-Aṣl (حكم الأصل)\nAl-ʿIllah / Al-Jāmiʿ (العلة / الجامع)\nAlthough all four are necessary, the most critical of them is the ʿillah, because Qiyās revolves around it. Without a valid ʿillah, there is no Qiyās.\nFollowed by Arkān (pillars), we discuss Masālik al-ʿIllah (Methods of Determining the ʿIllah)",
