        "overview": "This lesson examines an essential topic in uṣūl al-fiqh (legal theory): the methods of identifying the legal cause (ʿillah, عِلَّة) in qiyās (analogy). Specifically, it presents the Ḥanafī methodology in determining whether a particular attribute (waṣf, وَصْف) qualifies to function as an effective legal cause.\nThe Ḥanafī scholars developed a structured and rigorous two-stage process for validating a proposed ʿillah:\nṢalāḥ al-waṣf (صَلَاحُ الوَصْفِ): the suitability of the attribute\nTaʾthīr or ʿAdālah al-waṣf (تَأْثِيرُ الوَصْفِ / عَدَالَتُهُ): the effectiveness of the attribute",
